.TH HD-BASE 7 "October 2026" "hd-base" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-base \- the hyprdebian base system
.SH DESCRIPTION
The package
.B hd-base
depends on the packages that every hyprdebian system has, so that they are
installed with it and stay installed.
Besides the settings below, a package it pulls in is set up the way that
package does it.
.PP
It holds the parts that every hyprdebian system shares, each with a man page
of its own:
.TP
.BR hd-config (7)
The hyprdebian configuration,
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json ,
where hyprdebian packages keep their settings under a key of their own,
with
.BR hd-config-update (8)
and
.BR hd-config-remove (8).
.TP
.BR hd-network (7)
The network configuration:
.BR hd-network-render (8)
renders the
.BR systemd-networkd (8)
files from the key
.BR hd-network ,
in which
.BR hd-network-iface (8)
and
.BR hd-network-bridge (8)
change the interfaces and bridges, and the
.I .link
files that name ethernet and wifi interfaces by their path.
.TP
.BR hd-secboot (7)
The Secure Boot keys of the owner, which the postinst generates in
.I /etc/hyprdebian/secboot
when they are not there yet,
.BR hd-secboot-enroll (8),
which enrolls them in the firmware, and
.BR hd-secboot-check (8),
which checks that Secure Boot is on.
.PP
It installs
.BR hd-up (1),
which upgrades the system after a ZFS snapshot,
.BR hd-reboot (1)
and
.BR hd-poweroff (1),
which reboot and power off the system with
.B hyprshutdown
in a Hyprland session and with
.B systemctl
otherwise,
.BR hd-link-repo (8),
which switches the HyprDebian repository and suite of apt, and the files
that new users
get in their home directory, from
.IR /etc/skel ,
with
.BR hd-sync-skel (1),
which brings them into an existing home directory:
.TP
.I .bash_aliases
.B ls
and
.B ll
with
.BR eza (1),
.B y
for
.BR yazi (1),
.B wav2flac
which converts the
.I .wav
files below the current folder to
.I .flac
with
.BR ffmpeg (1)
and deletes them, and a history search on Ctrl-R with
.BR fzf (1).
.TP
.I .gitconfig
.BR delta (1)
as the pager and diff filter of
.BR git (1).
.TP
.I .config/nano/nanorc
Indents with four spaces, remembers the search history, and colors the
interface and the syntax.
.PP
It also sets up the system:
.TP
.I /etc/profile.d/local\-bin\-path.sh
Adds
.I ~/.local/bin
to the
.B PATH
of login shells, when that folder exists.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/preferences.d/00\-block\-unwanted
Keeps apt from installing
.BR ifupdown ,
as
.BR systemd-networkd (8)
runs the network,
.BR os-prober ,
and
.BR turnstile .
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/getty@.service.d/numlock.conf
Turns Num Lock on for a console before its login prompt shows, with
.BR setleds (1).
.TP
.I /etc/update\-motd.d/00\-hyprdebian
Shows the HyprDebian banner after a login on the console or over ssh, with
the version of HyprDebian from
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/version.json ,
the suite and the Debian version, the kernel, the uptime, the load, the
memory, the health of the ZFS pools and the RAID arrays, and the failed
units.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/zram\-generator.conf.d/hyprdebian.conf
A swap in compressed RAM,
.IR /dev/zram0 ,
of a quarter of the RAM, compressed with zstd, with priority 16384, so it is
used before the swap on disk; see
.BR zram-generator.conf (5).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/sysctl.d/50\-zram.conf
Sets
.B vm.swappiness
to 180, as swapping to zram is cheaper than dropping the page cache, and
.B vm.page\-cluster
to 0, as reading ahead does not help with zram.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/resolved.conf.d/00\-direct\-uplink.conf
Has
.BR systemd-resolved (8)
pass the queries straight to the name servers of the network: no stub
resolver on 127.0.0.53, no cache, no LLMNR, no multicast DNS and no fallback
servers.
.PP
Services are enabled on their installation as on Debian, by their presets,
see
.BR systemd.preset (5).
.PP
The postinst masks
.BR systemd-firstboot.service ,
.B rpcbind.socket
and
.B rpcbind.service
on the first installation; a unit that the admin unmasks again stays
unmasked on upgrades, and a purge unmasks them.
An upgrade from a version before 1.1 unmasks
.B systemd-preset-all.service
and
.BR systemd-machine-id-commit.service ,
which those versions masked as well, and renames the apt source
.IR /etc/apt/sources.list.d/hyprdebian.local.sources ,
the name of versions before 1.11, to
.IR hyprdebian.sources .
It also points
.I /etc/resolv.conf
at
.IR /run/systemd/resolve/resolv.conf ,
the name servers themselves, in place of the stub resolver, when it is the
link that
.B systemd-resolved
made.
When that file is missing, because
.B systemd-resolved
does not run, as in the chroot of the installer, it is made with the name
servers of the old link, so names keep resolving until
.B systemd-resolved
starts.
It empties
.IR /etc/motd ,
on the first installation like the masks, and diverts
.I /etc/update\-motd.d/10\-uname
of base-files to
.IR 10\-uname.base\-files ,
which
.BR run-parts (8)
skips, as the banner already shows the kernel; a removal of the package
puts it back.
It diverts
.I /etc/issue
of base-files to
.I /etc/issue.debian
and has
.BR hd-issue (8)
write the HyprDebian login banner there, with the version, the type and the
suite, on every installation and upgrade; a removal of the package puts the
banner of base-files back.
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/version.json
The version of HyprDebian, as
.B {"major": 1, "minor": 0}
for 1.0, which is also the version of
.BR hd-base .
The banners show it.
.SH PACKAGES
.TP
.B hyprdebian
.B python3
and
.BR sudo ,
for
.BR hd-up (1);
.BR python3-jinja2 ,
for
.BR hd-link-repo (8)
and
.BR hd-network-render (8);
.BR kbd ,
for Num Lock on the console.
.TP
.B Secure Boot
.BR openssl ,
.B efitools
and
.BR sbsigntool ,
which make the keys, enroll them and sign EFI files with them; see
.BR hd-secboot (7).
.TP
.B Remote access and firewall
.B openssh-server
and
.BR kitty-terminfo ,
so that the kitty terminal works over ssh;
.BR ufw ,
the firewall.
.TP
.B ZFS
.BR zfs-dkms ,
.B zfsutils-linux
and
.BR zfs-initramfs ;
.B build-essential
and
.B initramfs-tools
to build the ZFS module and the initrd.
.TP
.B Firmware and boot
.B firmware-linux
and
.BR firmware-qlogic ;
.B efibootmgr
for the boot entries of the firmware.
.TP
.B Console
.BR locales ,
.BR keyboard-configuration ,
.B console-setup
and
.BR ca-certificates .
.TP
.B System services
.BR systemd-resolved ,
name resolution.
The logs stay in the journal of
.BR systemd-journald (8);
there is no syslog daemon.
.TP
.B Command line tools
.BR eza ,
.BR fzf ,
.BR nfs-common ,
.BR psmisc ,
.BR net-tools ,
.BR pciutils ,
.BR usbutils ,
.BR acpi ,
.BR bash-completion ,
.BR git ,
.BR git-delta ,
.BR ack ,
.BR command-not-found ,
.BR man-db ,
.B apt-file
and
.BR systemd-zram-generator .
It conflicts with
.BR zram-tools ,
which would set up a second zram swap.
It replaces
.BR hd-config ,
.B hd-network
and
.BR hd-secboot ,
the packages that held the configuration, the network configuration and
the Secure Boot keys before; an upgrade removes them, and the configuration
and the keys stay.
.PP
.B firmware-linux
and
.B firmware-qlogic
are in the
.B non-free-firmware
component of Debian, which the apt sources must include.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/hd-up
Upgrades the system after a ZFS snapshot.
.TP
.I /usr/bin/hd-reboot
.TQ
.I /usr/bin/hd-poweroff
Reboot and power off the system.
.TP
.I /usr/bin/hd-sync-skel
Brings the files of
.I /etc/skel
into the home directory.
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/hd-issue
Writes the login banner in
.IR /etc/issue .
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/hd-link-repo
Switches the HyprDebian repository and suite of apt.
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/hd-config-update
.TQ
.I /usr/sbin/hd-config-remove
Change the hyprdebian configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/hd-network-render
.TQ
.I /usr/sbin/hd-network-iface
.TQ
.I /usr/sbin/hd-network-bridge
Render and change the network configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/hd-secboot-enroll
.TQ
.I /usr/sbin/hd-secboot-check
Enroll the Secure Boot keys and check that Secure Boot is on.
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
The hyprdebian configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/secboot
The Secure Boot keys.
.TP
.I /usr/share/hd-base/templates/hyprdebian.sources.j2
The template of the apt source of
.BR hd-link-repo .
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/version.json
The version of HyprDebian, a conffile.
.TP
.I /etc/skel/.bash_aliases
.TQ
.I /etc/skel/.gitconfig
.TQ
.I /etc/skel/.config/nano/nanorc
The files new users get, conffiles.
.TP
.I /etc/profile.d/local\-bin\-path.sh
Adds
.I ~/.local/bin
to the
.BR PATH ,
a conffile.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/preferences.d/00\-block\-unwanted
The packages apt never installs, a conffile.
.TP
.I /etc/update\-motd.d/00\-hyprdebian
The banner after a login, a conffile.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/getty@.service.d/numlock.conf
Num Lock on the console.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/zram\-generator.conf.d/hyprdebian.conf
The zram swap.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/sysctl.d/50\-zram.conf
The sysctls for the zram swap.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/resolved.conf.d/00\-direct\-uplink.conf
The config of systemd-resolved.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/network/10\-ethernet.link
.TQ
.I /usr/lib/systemd/network/20\-wifi.link
Name the network interfaces by their path.
